# compiler/tests/live/catching.expected: the cases of cases/ownership and of the quick gate's stdlib sample whose row of `F cases` differs
# under the catching convention (FIB_CATCH=all, which `--live` turns on: docs/design/live-repl.md 3.5) from the plain run, one DIR/CASE per
# line. stubs.sh fails on a difference that is not here and on a line here that no longer differs. Each line says why the header pins the
# non-catching behaviour.
# 8690: both jobs trap; without catching the process abandons the 14 objects the trapped tasks held (`audit: abandoned`, `leaks: 14`);
# a catching program unwinds a trapped task and releases them (audit clean, 0 leaks). The verdict is the convention's, not a stub's.
cases/stdlib/8690-compress-par-a-single-trapping-job-is-an-internal-error.fib
# 8643: an unjoined pool task traps; without catching the process abandons the 1 object its frames held (`audit: abandoned`, `leaks: 1`);
# a catching program unwinds the trapped task and releases it (audit clean, 0 leaks). It entered the sample when cases 4018, 4019 and
# 4208-4210 moved the sample's stride; the verdict is the convention's, not a stub's.
cases/stdlib/8643-an-unjoined-pool-task-that-traps-does-not-end-the-process.fib
# 8641: three pool tasks trap; without catching the process abandons the 8 objects their frames held (`audit: abandoned`, `leaks: 8`);
# a catching program unwinds the trapped tasks and releases them (audit clean, 0 leaks). The verdict is the convention's, not a stub's.
# In a catching program a non-worker joiner also runs a task it can claim (docs/design/parallelism.md 3.1, rt/park.lir
# fib.sched-claim-run), so which tasks the workers run depends on the schedule: the case counts the tasks a worker ran and checks
# `pool-tasks-run` (ctl 4) against that, so its result is 0 under every convention (CI 40233480544 saw the catching and the live
# tables disagree on the old check, `>= 4`, on a loaded 4-vCPU runner). It entered the sample when cases 4020 and 4021 moved the
# sample's stride and stays by this list.
cases/stdlib/8641-trap-in-a-pool-task-reaches-the-joiner-as-the-failure-of-that-task-and-the-siblings-finish.fib
